          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Section 5.2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.112,
            0.237,
            0.131
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 113**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.14,
            0.883,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": "**Q. How many prime numbers are there from 21 to 30? How many composite numbers are there from 21 to 30?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.187,
            0.506,
            0.233
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Prime numbers from 21 to 30: 2 (23,29) Composite numbers from 21 to 30: 8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.242,
            0.237,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 114**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.268,
            0.269,
            0.29
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.299,
            0.863,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": "**Q.1. We see that 2 is a prime and also an even number. Is there any other even prime?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.327,
            0.214,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": "Ans. No."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.354,
            0.881,
            0.39
          ],
          "content": "**Q.2. Look at the list of primes till 100. What is the smallest difference between two successive primes? What is the largest difference?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.399,
            0.882,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "Ans. The smallest difference between two successive primes is one (3-2=1) the largest difference is 8 (97-89)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.444,
            0.883,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Are there an equal number of primes occurring in every row in the table on the previous page? Which decades have the least number of primes? Which have the most number of primes?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.506,
            0.883,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "Ans. No. The least number of primes occur in the decades 91 to 100 and most number of primes and occur in the decades 1 to 10, 11 to 20."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.578,
            0.664,
            0.597
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Q.4. Which of the following numbers are prime: 23, 51, 37, 26?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.605,
            0.268,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "Ans. 23 and 37."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.632,
            0.828,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": "**Q.5. Write three pairs of prime numbers less than 20 whose sum is a multiple of 5.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.659,
            0.741,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Pairs of prime numbers less than 20 whose sum is a multiple of 5 are (2,3), (3,7), (2,13) (Try for other possibilities)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.741,
            0.881,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "**Q.6. The numbers 13 and 31 are prime numbers. Both these numbers have same digits 1 and 3. Find such pairs of prime numbers up to 100.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.786,
            0.447,
            0.805
          ],
          "content": "Ans. 17 and 71, 37 and 73, 79 and 97."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.841,
            0.701,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "**Q.7. Find seven consecutive composite numbers between 1 and 100.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.867,
            0.391,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "Ans. 90, 91, 92, 93, 94, 95, 96."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.493,
            0.928,
            0.506,
            0.939
          ],
          "content": "4"
        }
      ]
    }
